Quake II's Linux port forces gl_finish 1 in R_Init, after the config and the
+set command line, so a glFinish ends every frame's R_RenderView: the CPU
waits for the GPU to finish before it builds the next frame and the two
never overlap. Probably a work-around for the 3dfx era; with a current
driver it only costs frames (CI20 SGX540, q2demo1: 14.4 -> 15.4 fps without
it). The cvar keeps its default of 0 and can still be set.

	if (gl_finish->value)
		qglFinish ();

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/src/gl_rmain.c	2026-11-24 12:15:09.873915148 +0100
+++ b/src/gl_rmain.c	2026-11-24 12:15:09.883791618 +0100
@@ -1247,10 +1247,6 @@ qboolean R_Init( void *hinstance, void *
 		ri.Cvar_Set( "scr_drawall", "0" );
 	}
 
-#ifdef __linux__
-	ri.Cvar_SetValue( "gl_finish", 1 );
-#endif
-
 	// MCD has buffering issues
 	if ( gl_config.renderer == GL_RENDERER_MCD )
 	{
